  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the given reaction</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/777ef96f-95da-4cba-8803-c427d3e71597.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 130px;\" /></p><p>The, total number of possible products formed by tertiary carbocation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>There are two tertiary carbocations possible due to rearrangement of hydride or methyl groups. Totally four structural alkene products are formed, out of which one is having chiral centre. Hence, total number of products formed through the formation of carbocation intermediate are 5.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/42ae39f5-4c75-4110-ba61-a905ec23434d.png\" style=\"width: 508px; height: 455px;\" /></p><p>(Total 5&nbsp;products are possible through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> carbocation)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
